 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nIndex parameter parsing broken after recent changes\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `_parse_index_params` method appears to have a parsing issue where the method returns early before processing all index parameters. This causes index creation statements to fail parsing correctly.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\n\n# This should parse correctly but fails\nsql = \"CREATE INDEX idx ON table_name (column1, column2) USING btree\"\nparsed = sqlglot.parse_one(sql)\nprint(parsed)\n```\n\nThe parser seems to return from `_parse_index_params` before processing the `columns`, `include`, `with_storage`, and `using` parameters that come after the initial parsing of `partition_by`, `where`, and `on` clauses.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nIndex creation statements should parse all parameters correctly, including column specifications, USING clauses, INCLUDE clauses, and WITH storage options.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\nThe parser appears to exit the `_parse_index_params` method prematurely, leaving important index parameters unprocessed.\n</issue>\n",
